@startuml
title Link an account, sync it, then read the dashboard
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 15
skinparam maxMessageSize 180
actor User
participant "Browser + Next.js proxy" as UI
participant "FastAPI" as API
participant "Plaid service" as Service
participant "Plaid Sandbox" as Plaid
database "App SQLite" as DB
User -> UI : Connect a bank
UI -> API : POST /plaid/link-token
API -> Plaid : create_link_token(user UUID)
Plaid --> UI : link_token (through API)
UI -> Plaid : Open Plaid Link\ncredentials stay with Plaid
Plaid --> UI : public_token
UI -> API : POST /plaid/exchange
API -> Plaid : exchange public_token
Plaid --> API : access_token + item_id
API -> DB : Store Fernet-encrypted token\ncommit item before sync
API -> Service : sync_item
Service -> Plaid : /transactions/sync\nall pages from saved cursor
Plaid --> Service : added + modified + removed\nnext_cursor
Service -> DB : Upsert / soft-remove transactions\ncommit rows + cursor together
Service -> Plaid : /accounts/balance/get\n/liabilities/get
Service -> DB : Refresh balances and debts
API --> UI : item_id + synced true/false
note over API, DB
Sync failure keeps the linked item.
User can retry POST /plaid/items/{id}/sync.
end note
UI -> API : GET /dashboard
API -> DB : Read saved accounts + liabilities
API --> UI : Net worth + balances + debts
== Later transaction updates ==
Plaid -> API : POST /plaid/webhook\nSYNC_UPDATES_AVAILABLE
API --> Plaid : 200 quickly
API -> Service : Background sync_transactions
Service -> DB : Update transactions + cursor
note over Service, DB
Webhook refreshes transactions only.
Balances, liabilities and budget evaluation
need their own refresh / run.
end note
@enduml
